# Points 4, 5, 7 of the verification order, 2026-11-18.

=== 4a. mirrored pair order (render the LATER frame against an EARLIER reference)
BEFORE  violet d1 0.108% / d2 0.167%      chainsaw d1 0.000% / d2 nan
AFTER   violet d1 0.095% / d2 0.168%      chainsaw d1 0.000% / d2 nan

=== 4b. control_max <= sweep_max still fails, and why
  probe fp16 control on its 13 pairs: chainsaw 0.083%, violet 0.077%
  full fp16 sweep:                    chainsaw 0.07546%, violet 0.07345%
  a max over a subset cannot exceed the max over the set -> the probe's pairs are NOT a subset of
  the render's reuses: the probe re-decides the gate on its own decoded frames instead of replaying
  the render's decisions. Mirroring removed the direction cause; the decision replay is the other.

=== 5. frame 475 is the same level, not a level mismatch
  share>4 0.45534%, share>6 0.13860%, share>8 0.07108%  (vs the closest earlier frame, 474)
  the gate's recorded delta for 475: 0.07108%  -> level 8, identical
  so 0.07108 > 0.07 is a simulation/product difference of 1.6% in the statistic, not a level mix-up

=== 7a. discard rate in adversarial selection: 0 of 13 = 0% (valid by the 20% rule)

=== 7b. block-max as a second condition
  render with --temporal_reuse_block_max 8 on Chainsaw 20 s: 83/481 reused (17.3%) - identical to
  the share-only gate, so the condition is free there.
  over the channel-max gate's 78 reuses (replay): none has a block-max above 3.0 except 2, and there
  are no frames above the bar left to catch - the condition buys nothing on this clip.
  Its value is structural: it bounds the per-block delta, which the share does not.

=== 5b. the depth table cannot be produced on the sweep's population
  the sweep is over the product's 83 reuses; the depth table comes from a replay (78 reuses), because
  the render logs no per-frame depth. The two differ by 5 frames and the replay's max HR (0.07489%) is
  not the sweep's (0.07546%): the worst frame, 475, is a MISS in the replay (its share 0.07108 > 0.07)
  and a reuse in the product. So "the worst frame is a depth-1 reuse" is supported by the replay's
  population, not by the render's. Closing this needs the render to log (frame, depth, reference).
